  "readmeFile": "PACKAGE.md",
  "releaseNotes": "A security update for hosts that compile or run untrusted queries, and a new opt-in execution limit.\nRequires PhoenixmlDb.Core 2.6.0.\n\n### New: a limit on the length of a built string\n\n`QueryExecutionLimits.MaxStringLength` (`int?`, default `null`: no limit) sets the longest string,\nin UTF-16 code units, that one operation may build. An operation that goes past it fails with\n`FOER0000`, the code of the other execution limits; a query can catch it with `try`/`catch`.\n\n- It applies to `fn:concat`, `fn:string-join`, the `||` operator, string constructors,\n  `fn:codepoints-to-string`, `fn:replace`, `fn:serialize`, `fn:xml-to-json`, `fn:upper-case`,\n  `fn:lower-case`, `fn:encode-for-uri`, `fn:escape-html-uri`, `fn:iri-to-uri`,\n  `fn:normalize-unicode`, and the text that node constructors join.\n- `fn:string-join`, `fn:replace`, string constructors and node constructors stop before the\n  string passes the limit, so they do not allocate the full string.\n- The limit is per string, not per query. `MaxResultItems` limits materialized sequences.\n- `QueryExecutionContext.CheckStringLength(long)` applies the same limit in host code and\n  extension functions.\n\nA time limit alone cannot stop an expression that builds a very large string from no input. A\nhost that runs untrusted queries sets both.\n\n### Security: import location hints with no base URI (GHSA-52r3-6pq9-42m5)\n\nOnly hosts that compile queries from untrusted parties are affected.\n\n- **A relative import location hint with no base URI is not resolved against the working\n  directory.** In a query compiled with no base URI:\n  - `import schema ... at 'x.xsd'` gives XQST0059, with and without a `ResourcePolicy`. Under a\n    policy whose file roots hold the working directory, 3.0.0 resolves the hint against the\n    working directory and reads the file there.\n  - `import module ... at 'm.xqm'` gives XQST0059, with and without a `ResourcePolicy`. 3.0.0 reads\n    `m.xqm` from the working directory: with no policy, and under a policy whose file roots hold\n    the working directory.\n\n  With a base URI, a relative hint resolves against it. A host that compiles a query with no\n  base URI and imports a module or schema from the working directory by a relative hint gives the\n  working directory as the base URI (`CompilationOptions.BaseUri`). The `xquery` CLI does this.\n  A location that the host maps (`ExternalModuleLocations`, `ExternalModules`) or supplies through\n  its resource resolver does not change.\n\n### Also in this release\n\n- **A prefixed name parses in linear time** (#363): a query with 10,000 calls such as `fn:abs(1)`\n  compiles in 0.19 s.\n- **A sequence of long paths compiles** (#360): the sum of the cardinality estimates is clamped,\n  so the cost model does not overflow.\n- **The library builds with .NET SDK 10.0.401 and later** under warnings as errors: three\n  `default(T)` expressions that IDE0034 reports are simplified. No compiled code changes.\n\n### `xquery` CLI (ships on `cli-v3.1.0`)\n\n- Runs on **PhoenixmlDb.XQuery 3.1.0** and **PhoenixmlDb.Xslt 3.1.0**, so it includes the\n  fixes above and `fn:transform` from a query gets the 3.1.0 engine.\n- Includes the fix for GHSA-52r3-6pq9-42m5 (see above).",
